THE BACKGROUND OF DELTANIA

Deltania is an old kingdom, and its roads remember it.  Itrius, the
capitol on the eastern road, has been sacked twice, chartered once,
and beautified against its will.  Around it: the Kobold Caves, which
the crown pretends are empty; the Goblin Outpost in the southern
forest, which the crown pretends does not exist; Castle in Ruins,
where King Uther's line waits out an argument with the weather; and
the Mountain Ruins, which nobody pretends about at all.

To the west the great surface map runs to the Dragon Sea: Locris
Ferry on the river, the Jhaden forests, the Zargos mountains, and
the Great Eastern Desert, which is exactly as pleasant as advertised.

Deities take an interest, the weather is an armed combatant, and the
trolls of the southern manner send complaint letters written entirely
in swear words.  It is, in short, home.
